    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "What is it like to work in "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Antarctica",
            "zh": "南极洲"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "? Port Lockroy is a "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "research",
            "ref": "v-research"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " station there. It "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "draws",
            "zh": "吸引"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " 18,000 visitors every year. It is one of Antarctica’s most visited places."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Port Lockroy sits on Goudier "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "Island",
            "ref": "v-island"
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "",
            "zh": "古迪尔岛"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". The island is small. It is about the size of a football "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "field",
            "ref": "v-field"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". It is home to 2,000 gentoo "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "penguins",
            "ref": "v-penguin"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". The port also "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "houses",
            "ref": "v-house"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the world’s "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "southernmost",
            "zh": "最南端的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " post office."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Four people work at Lockroy each year from November to March. They help "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "count",
            "ref": "v-count"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the penguins. They work at the post office. They also "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "run",
            "zh": "经营"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " a gift shop."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "It’s very cold in Antarctica. Sometimes, you might not get a "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "shower",
            "zh": "淋浴"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " for days. Would you like to live and work there?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      },
      {
        "id": "n1",
        "type": "note",
        "title": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Did you know?"
          }
        ],
        "content": [
          [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "*洛克罗伊港（Port Lockroy），建于1944年，曾是第二次世界大战时期的英国基地，之后在1996年被改造成一座博物馆。该港还被用于开展南极科考工作。"
            }
          ]
        ]
      }
    ],
